Z||000016||JMergen||11-04-2000||01:41 AM||||stsmithgt, Your trunk clearance theory may be correct, but I was told that the Super Bird wing was developed from wind tunnell datta. IE for a "wing" to function as a wing it must be up out of the turbulant air that flows over the rear of the car, otherwise the "wing" functions as a spoiler.||||reg||1
Z||000017||theogre||11-04-2000||09:34 PM||||Since we've digressed so far already,,,,, Superbird was build entirely to run in NASCAR. They only made enough of them to meet NASCAR production rules. Anyting you wanted on the race car had to be available on the street car. Superbird wasn't the only car like that but it was definatly the one that stands out most for the majority of people. (I think the original Chrysler 300 was along the same lines.)<P>||||reg||1
